 "note": "Saltwater, the Busselton Performing Arts and Convention Centre (City of Busselton, Kerry Hill Architects; opened May 2026), 9 Queen St, on the east side of Queen St between Marine Tce and the Weld Theatre, opposite the Old Courthouse. Not in OSM. From the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026) only: no usable photo of the finished building was found, so the massing is measured and the finishes are a sober guess. A flat-roofed group about 55 m along Queen St by 41 m deep: a low glazed gallery and foyer band along the street under a cantilevered canopy, the tall auditorium and fly tower in the south half, the three-level conference block in the north-west corner with its level 2 balcony looking north to the bay, a plant deck between them and a lower service band along the back and the south. Name in plain lettering, no logo. Metres: x left to right as seen from Queen St (north to south), y back (east) from the front glazing.",
